This distribution includes research software, synthetic demonstrations,
validation summaries, and the published V3.2 model artifact, including
deidentified calibration geometry arrays. It does not include raw clinical
records, source clinical images, linkage maps, or direct patient identifiers.

The software and model identify biometric configurations that are unusual
relative to an internal single-center reference. They do not diagnose disease,
select an intraocular lens formula, establish postoperative accuracy, or replace
clinical judgment. The package is research and education software and has not
been cleared or approved as a medical device.
